---
description: >-
  Markup, entities and both quote kinds in every text c4-beta draws or
  writes as an attribute or accessible text: title, accTitle, a multi-line
  accDescr, names, a description, a technology, instances and a relation
  label. Tags are drawn as written (#1440), so the node's header is wide:
  the plain container db widens the node, so that the header slides clear
  of the relation in TB instead of being crossed by it. The person colour
  from the c4 section is
  legacy C4's: c4-beta never reads it, so the person keeps its theme
  colours and nothing is written from the key or warned of.
config:
  c4:
    person_bg_color: 'red" onload="alert(1)'
---
c4-beta deployment
title <script>alert(1)</script> "Title" & 'more'
accTitle: <b onmouseover="x()">Acc</b> "title" & 'more'
accDescr {
  </desc><script>alert(2)</script>
  "Description" & 'more' <img src=x onerror=y()>
}
person user "<svg onload=z()>User</svg>" "Says \"hi\" & 'bye'"
deploymentNode node "Node <i>one</i>" "Runs it" "<a href='javascript:q()'>Tech</a>" instances "<b>3</b> & \"x\"" {
  container db "DB"
  container api "API &lt;b&gt;" "Serves </text><text>orders" "Kotlin <br> JVM"
}
user --> api : "Calls <script>s()</script> \"now\"" "HTTPS & 'TLS'"
